msgid "This start-up partition still holds Windows Boot Manager and its settings, but the settings list no system to start: the Windows they belonged to is gone, or its entry was removed. Nothing is damaged. "
msgstr "This start-up partition still holds Windows Boot Manager and its settings, but the settings list no system to start: the Windows they belonged to is gone, or its entry was removed. Nothing is damaged. "

msgid "The PC's start-up list tries this partition first, shows an error, and only then goes on to the next choice."
msgstr "The PC's start-up list tries this partition first, shows an error, and only then goes on to the next choice."

msgid "This PC does not start from this partition, so the files do no harm where they are."
msgstr "This PC does not start from this partition, so the files do no harm where they are."

msgid " If the PC is ever started from Disk "
msgstr " If the PC is ever started from Disk "

msgid ", it shows a start-up error instead of a system.\n\nYou can leave the files, or remove them to tidy up. If an entry was removed by mistake, Undo in the backups list brings it back."
msgstr ", it shows a start-up error instead of a system.\n\nYou can leave the files, or remove them to tidy up. If an entry was removed by mistake, Undo in the backups list brings it back."

msgid "Damaged start-up settings on "
msgstr "Damaged start-up settings on "

msgid "\n\nNo Windows found on this PC starts through this partition, so these are leftover files. Removing them is safe."
msgstr "\n\nNo Windows found on this PC starts through this partition, so these are leftover files. Removing them is safe."

msgid "\n\nNo Windows found on this PC uses these settings. If a Windows should start from this disk, it was not found: check that its disk is connected and unlocked."
msgstr "\n\nNo Windows found on this PC uses these settings. If a Windows should start from this disk, it was not found: check that its disk is connected and unlocked."

msgid "the partition it points to is not on any disk now"
msgstr "the partition it points to is not on any disk now"

msgid "A start-up entry points to a drive locked by BitLocker: \""
msgstr "A start-up entry points to a drive locked by BitLocker: \""

msgid "The start-up menu on {0} lists \"{1}\" on {2}, but that drive is encrypted with BitLocker and locked, so it cannot be checked. Windows is very likely inside it.\n\nDo not remove this entry. Unlock the drive first (with its 48-digit recovery key) and scan again: only then can it be seen whether the entry is fine."
msgstr "The start-up menu on {0} lists \"{1}\" on {2}, but that drive is encrypted with BitLocker and locked, so it cannot be checked. Windows is very likely inside it.\n\nDo not remove this entry. Unlock the drive first (with its 48-digit recovery key) and scan again: only then can it be seen whether the entry is fine."

msgid "BitLocker encrypts a whole drive. While it is locked, no program can see the Windows inside it, so a working start-up entry looks as if it leads nowhere."
msgstr "BitLocker encrypts a whole drive. While it is locked, no program can see the Windows inside it, so a working start-up entry looks as if it leads nowhere."

msgid "there is no Windows in "
msgstr "there is no Windows in "

